            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation and management of adult shoulder pain: a focus on rotator cuff disorders, acromioclavicular joint arthritis, and glenohumeral arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>755-75, xii</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.mcna.2014.03.004</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0025-7125(14)00043-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Shoulder pain is a common reason for a patient to see their primary care physician. This article focuses on the evaluation and management of 3 common shoulder disorders; rotator cuff disorders, acromioclavicular joint arthritis, and glenohumeral joint arthritis. The typical history and physical examination findings for each of these entities are highlighted, in addition to treatment options.</AbstractText>
